1
00:00:01,292 --> 00:00:08,174
Oh, Mister Tailor… ♪
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

2
00:00:09,592 --> 00:00:10,802
♪ Oh, Mister Tailor ♪

3
00:00:10,885 --> 00:00:12,637
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

4
00:00:12,721 --> 00:00:16,683
♪ One cut, and it’s over ♪

5
00:00:16,766 --> 00:00:18,935
Atoy: November 14, 2026.

6
00:00:19,019 --> 00:00:22,021
The Washer will come to this place

7
00:00:22,105 --> 00:00:24,149
and they'll have a transaction there.

8
00:00:24,232 --> 00:00:25,358
Uno: I'll make it up to you, Sir.

9
00:00:25,442 --> 00:00:27,694
I'll get better so I can assist
you on this mission.

10
00:00:27,777 --> 00:00:28,862
I trust you, Uno.

11
00:00:28,945 --> 00:00:30,280
I know where…

12
00:00:30,363 --> 00:00:32,741
Elvis and Rochelle hang out.

13
00:00:33,283 --> 00:00:34,951
Paldo: You'll see,
later we'll have evidence.

14
00:00:35,035 --> 00:00:35,952
Gotcha!

15
00:00:36,036 --> 00:00:36,703
Hey, Miss.

16
00:00:36,786 --> 00:00:37,871
Atoy: What were…

17
00:00:37,954 --> 00:00:39,330
the things injected into him?

18
00:00:39,414 --> 00:00:41,082
Nurse: They can't identify it.

19
00:00:41,166 --> 00:00:44,169
Didn't you say you and
Ibyang are fraternal twins?

20
00:00:44,252 --> 00:00:45,587
Yes. Why?

21
00:00:45,670 --> 00:00:48,089
How did that happen? You're adopted.

22
00:00:48,173 --> 00:00:50,759
Liar, liar, pants on fire.

23
00:00:50,842 --> 00:00:52,802
[laughing] [music continues]

24
00:00:52,886 --> 00:00:54,596
How did they find out?

25
00:00:54,679 --> 00:00:55,722
It was Ibyang!

26
00:00:55,805 --> 00:00:58,391
It feels like we've met somewhere before?

27
00:00:58,933 --> 00:00:59,684
At the bar!

28
00:00:59,768 --> 00:01:01,186
Maybe, maybe. [chuckles softly]

29
00:01:01,269 --> 00:01:01,811
Yes.

30
00:01:01,895 --> 00:01:03,063
- Ah, Georgia.
- Georgia: You seem…

31
00:01:03,146 --> 00:01:03,980
Rommel.

32
00:01:04,064 --> 00:01:05,190
Go greet your aunt Cita.

33
00:01:05,273 --> 00:01:06,983
- Hi, Aunt Cita.
- Hi, Rommel!

34
00:01:07,067 --> 00:01:08,902
- Ah-
- Papa has told me stories about you.

35
00:01:08,985 --> 00:01:10,153
Gavin!

36
00:01:10,236 --> 00:01:11,988
Oh my gosh! It's you!

37
00:01:12,072 --> 00:01:13,364
- Ah, wait.
- Shocks!

38
00:01:13,448 --> 00:01:16,576
I kept calling you at the run,
but you kept ignoring me!

39
00:01:16,659 --> 00:01:17,869
What are you doing here?

40
00:01:17,952 --> 00:01:18,578
Chanty: What's wrong?

41
00:01:18,661 --> 00:01:20,163
Hey. Atoy?

42
00:01:20,789 --> 00:01:23,333
Atoy: Nothing, we weren't supposed
to be in that picture.

43
00:01:23,416 --> 00:01:25,084
Are you sure? Is that all?

44
00:01:25,627 --> 00:01:26,336
Yes.

45
00:01:26,419 --> 00:01:28,254
- Emerson: Atoy, really now?
- You seem to be doubting me.

46
00:01:28,338 --> 00:01:30,632
The whole dance club knows I'm adopted!

47
00:01:30,715 --> 00:01:32,926
Hailey is lying!

48
00:01:33,009 --> 00:01:34,928
Janine: Don't deny it anymore, Ibyang!

49
00:01:35,011 --> 00:01:36,930
It’s perfectly safe now. Okay, okay.

50
00:01:37,013 --> 00:01:38,515
Hey. Sorry, sorry…

51
00:01:39,098 --> 00:01:39,933
Emerson, sorry.

52
00:01:40,016 --> 00:01:41,059
Audrey: What is that?

53
00:01:42,519 --> 00:01:43,186
Let me see.

54
00:01:43,269 --> 00:01:44,896
It's just trash- it's nothing!

55
00:01:44,979 --> 00:01:45,605
It's nothing.

56
00:01:45,688 --> 00:01:47,106
Why don't you want to show me?

57
00:01:47,190 --> 00:01:48,399
[music continues]

58
00:01:48,483 --> 00:01:49,567
Audrey.

59
00:01:49,651 --> 00:01:50,485
What is this?

60
00:01:58,076 --> 00:02:00,703
[music swells]

61
00:02:01,788 --> 00:02:04,290
Who is this woman with Atoy?

62
00:02:04,374 --> 00:02:06,668
[suspicious music playing]

63
00:02:06,751 --> 00:02:07,752
I don't know her.

64
00:02:07,836 --> 00:02:10,088
[music continues]

65
00:02:10,171 --> 00:02:11,131
But is that really Atoy?

66
00:02:11,214 --> 00:02:12,132
Maybe it's…

67
00:02:13,174 --> 00:02:14,050
someone else.

68
00:02:14,717 --> 00:02:16,094
It's blurry, look.

69
00:02:16,177 --> 00:02:18,596
I know my husband's face by heart.

70
00:02:19,305 --> 00:02:19,931
It's him.

71
00:02:21,266 --> 00:02:23,434
I'm the one who bought that coat!

72
00:02:25,645 --> 00:02:28,439
Well, we can't be sure
the picture is real, Audrey.

73
00:02:28,523 --> 00:02:29,607
Because there's…

74
00:02:29,691 --> 00:02:32,193
AI now, so maybe that's AI.

75
00:02:32,861 --> 00:02:36,406
I know what's AI and what isn't, Oka.

76
00:02:40,785 --> 00:02:41,578
Oh, where are you going?

77
00:02:41,661 --> 00:02:43,288
To my wonderful husband!

78
00:02:43,371 --> 00:02:44,789
Audrey, wa--

79
00:02:44,873 --> 00:02:50,545
[tense music playing]

80
00:02:51,629 --> 00:02:52,714
[music fades]

81
00:02:54,132 --> 00:02:58,136
[theme music playing]

82
00:02:58,219 --> 00:03:00,430
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor… ♪

83
00:03:00,513 --> 00:03:05,852
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

84
00:03:06,519 --> 00:03:08,229
♪ Wait a moment, Mr. Tailor ♪

85
00:03:08,313 --> 00:03:10,148
♪ Can you be the one to stitch up ♪

86
00:03:10,231 --> 00:03:13,610
♪ The hole in my polo that's
right under the armpit ♪

87
00:03:13,693 --> 00:03:16,279
♪ In every cut of cloth ♪

88
00:03:16,362 --> 00:03:17,864
♪ There’s a secret behind it ♪

89
00:03:17,947 --> 00:03:19,782
♪ If your measurement is wrong,

90
00:03:19,866 --> 00:03:24,120
the whole fit turns crooked… ♪

91
00:03:24,203 --> 00:03:25,455
[gunshots]

92
00:03:25,538 --> 00:03:26,873
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor ♪

93
00:03:26,956 --> 00:03:29,042
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

94
00:03:29,125 --> 00:03:31,127
[music swells]

95
00:03:33,087 --> 00:03:34,422
[music fades]

96
00:03:36,382 --> 00:03:39,510
- Hey, Ru-- Rudy, behave!
- I'm ticklish there, you know?

97
00:03:39,594 --> 00:03:40,887
[chuckles] You're so fidgety.

98
00:03:40,970 --> 00:03:42,722
- I can't-- behave, okay-
- Well, I'm ticklish, you know.

99
00:03:42,805 --> 00:03:44,474
- I'm ticklish.
- What? Wa-- wait.

100
00:03:44,557 --> 00:03:45,892
- I'm ticklish-
- Godmother?

101
00:03:45,975 --> 00:03:47,477
Oh, Atoy.

102
00:03:48,895 --> 00:03:51,648
Ah, do you-- do you need help?

103
00:03:51,731 --> 00:03:54,275
Ah, no. It's fine. I can do this.

104
00:03:54,359 --> 00:03:55,568
Atoy: Ah, okay.

105
00:03:55,652 --> 00:03:57,570
[both chuckle softly]

106
00:03:57,654 --> 00:03:58,279
Ah…

107
00:04:00,031 --> 00:04:01,532
So you're Atoy.

108
00:04:01,616 --> 00:04:05,662
Ah, your Godmother Cita told me about you,

109
00:04:05,745 --> 00:04:06,329
that…

110
00:04:06,412 --> 00:04:08,331
you own this tailoring shop.

111
00:04:08,414 --> 00:04:09,374
Yes.

112
00:04:09,457 --> 00:04:10,833
By the way, I'm Rudy.

113
00:04:10,917 --> 00:04:13,002
- Hi. I’m Atoy.
- Rudy Romero.

114
00:04:13,086 --> 00:04:17,674
So, you've known
Godmother Cita for a long time?

115
00:04:17,757 --> 00:04:20,677
Ah, yes. Ah, actually, we have a…

116
00:04:20,760 --> 00:04:22,345
past, Cita and I.

117
00:04:22,428 --> 00:04:23,513
Hey, come on.

118
00:04:23,596 --> 00:04:24,305
- That was a long time ago.
- What?

119
00:04:24,389 --> 00:04:26,391
Ah, Atoy, we were just kids back then.

120
00:04:26,474 --> 00:04:27,892
Rudy: Mmm-mmm.

121
00:04:27,976 --> 00:04:29,185
- Ah-
- Cita: Ah--

122
00:04:29,269 --> 00:04:30,853
One of the best times of my life

123
00:04:30,937 --> 00:04:33,356
was when I met Cita.

124
00:04:33,439 --> 00:04:37,485
It sounds like you two might want
to extend those best times, ah.

125
00:04:38,486 --> 00:04:39,946
Hey, Atoy, nothing like that.

126
00:04:40,029 --> 00:04:43,783
Rudy here is just having a suit made.

127
00:04:43,866 --> 00:04:44,867
He isn't saying anything like that.

128
00:04:44,951 --> 00:04:46,035
Really?

129
00:04:46,119 --> 00:04:47,704
Have you taken his measurements yet?

130
00:04:47,787 --> 00:04:49,998
Ah, not yet, not yet.

131
00:04:50,081 --> 00:04:50,707
We're not done yet.

132
00:04:50,790 --> 00:04:51,291
Ah, oh, okay, okay.

133
00:04:51,374 --> 00:04:52,542
- Wait a minute, okay.
- Here. Yes. Okay, okay. Ah--

134
00:04:53,167 --> 00:04:54,002
Waist.

135
00:04:54,085 --> 00:04:55,503
[light music playing]

136
00:04:56,713 --> 00:04:57,547
Can you manage, Godmother?

137
00:04:57,630 --> 00:04:58,339
Cita: Yes, yes.

138
00:04:58,423 --> 00:04:58,965
I can do this.

139
00:04:59,048 --> 00:04:59,590
All right.

140
00:04:59,674 --> 00:05:00,550
I'm not even breathing anymore.

141
00:05:00,633 --> 00:05:01,551
Yes, okay.

142
00:05:02,510 --> 00:05:04,095
Cita: There. That's right, isn't it?

143
00:05:04,178 --> 00:05:05,138
[music fades]

144
00:05:05,221 --> 00:05:06,639
So, bro, what's the explanation?

145
00:05:06,723 --> 00:05:08,099
Huh? Why does Chanty know me?

146
00:05:08,182 --> 00:05:09,058
You're the one she's talking to.

147
00:05:09,142 --> 00:05:10,143
Why doesn't she know you?

148
00:05:11,185 --> 00:05:12,812
Well, bro, don't get mad, okay.

149
00:05:13,313 --> 00:05:13,855
What?

150
00:05:15,106 --> 00:05:18,609
I used your picture when
I was chatting with Chanty.

151
00:05:18,693 --> 00:05:19,319
Huh?!

152
00:05:20,153 --> 00:05:21,863
Bro, chill, calm down.

153
00:05:21,946 --> 00:05:22,864
Bro, what do you mean “chill”?

154
00:05:22,947 --> 00:05:24,282
Why would I chill?

155
00:05:24,365 --> 00:05:26,576
What you're doing is wrong,
that's catfishing!

156
00:05:26,659 --> 00:05:27,410
[scoffs]

157
00:05:27,493 --> 00:05:28,578
- I know that-
- And why did you need

158
00:05:28,661 --> 00:05:29,996
to pretend I'm you?

159
00:05:30,079 --> 00:05:31,748
Well, bro, I'm sorry.

160
00:05:31,831 --> 00:05:33,583
You know that…

161
00:05:33,666 --> 00:05:34,834
Chanty won't talk to me

162
00:05:34,917 --> 00:05:37,211
if she finds out I'm the
one she's talking to.

163
00:05:37,295 --> 00:05:38,671
Who am I anyway?

164
00:05:38,755 --> 00:05:40,673
I'm a benchwarmer on the team, right?

165
00:05:40,757 --> 00:05:42,258
And you…you're the MVP.

166
00:05:42,341 --> 00:05:44,343
Bro, you can improve, you know.

167
00:05:45,094 --> 00:05:46,679
And your identity isn't just about

168
00:05:46,763 --> 00:05:47,847
the basketball team.

169
00:05:47,930 --> 00:05:49,265
You're decent.

170
00:05:49,766 --> 00:05:52,351
Gavin: You just really lack confidence.

171
00:05:52,977 --> 00:05:54,645
Bro, you need to tell Chanty the truth.

172
00:05:55,354 --> 00:05:57,356
If you like her, start it right.

173
00:05:57,440 --> 00:05:58,608
Bro, I'm not ready yet.

174
00:05:58,691 --> 00:06:00,443
And I won't drag this out.

175
00:06:01,027 --> 00:06:02,862
I'll take care of it.

176
00:06:02,945 --> 00:06:04,739
[pensive music playing]

177
00:06:07,658 --> 00:06:08,493
Oh, I know!

178
00:06:09,077 --> 00:06:10,203
I've thought of a way.

179
00:06:11,287 --> 00:06:13,456
You need to hurt Chanty.

180
00:06:13,539 --> 00:06:15,458
And once you've hurt her,

181
00:06:15,541 --> 00:06:16,417
you'll break up with her.

182
00:06:17,001 --> 00:06:17,502
Right?

183
00:06:18,252 --> 00:06:19,921
And, well, once you hurt her,

184
00:06:20,004 --> 00:06:21,547
I'll be her comfort person.

185
00:06:21,631 --> 00:06:22,965
No way. No way.

186
00:06:23,049 --> 00:06:24,133
Karla will get mad at me

187
00:06:24,217 --> 00:06:25,259
if she finds out I broke up with

188
00:06:25,343 --> 00:06:26,177
Chanty.

189
00:06:26,260 --> 00:06:28,221
Karla doesn't need
to know about this, bro.

190
00:06:28,304 --> 00:06:30,056
Just trust me.

191
00:06:30,139 --> 00:06:31,474
Please, come on.

192
00:06:31,557 --> 00:06:33,226
Come on, it's me, you know.

193
00:06:33,309 --> 00:06:34,268
What is this, bro--

194
00:06:34,352 --> 00:06:35,853
I'll help you with your research paper

195
00:06:35,937 --> 00:06:37,188
and economics.

196
00:06:37,271 --> 00:06:38,981
Oh, didn't Coach say so?

197
00:06:39,065 --> 00:06:41,776
Before you play,
you need to pass economics.

198
00:06:41,859 --> 00:06:42,985
I'll take care of you.

199
00:06:44,946 --> 00:06:45,738
Rommel: Come on.

200
00:06:48,616 --> 00:06:49,408
Oh, okay.

201
00:06:50,284 --> 00:06:51,744
As long as you take care
of my assignments, okay.

202
00:06:51,828 --> 00:06:53,871
Deal. Thanks, bro.

203
00:06:53,955 --> 00:06:54,872
[phone blips]

204
00:06:56,040 --> 00:06:59,585
[rousing music playing]

205
00:07:00,336 --> 00:07:04,715
[soft rock music playing]

206
00:07:05,633 --> 00:07:08,427
Miss Cita is so lucky!

207
00:07:08,970 --> 00:07:10,304
Her ex is trying to win her back,

208
00:07:10,388 --> 00:07:12,432
traveling all the way to Baclaran!

209
00:07:12,515 --> 00:07:13,266
You’re the one, Miss Cita!

210
00:07:13,349 --> 00:07:14,642
Ame, it’s nothing like that.

211
00:07:14,725 --> 00:07:16,102
- Stop teasing me.
- Hmm?

212
00:07:16,769 --> 00:07:17,687
No, really, Godmother.

213
00:07:18,229 --> 00:07:20,106
Did you not feel any…

214
00:07:20,189 --> 00:07:21,816
spark, like a bubble?

215
00:07:21,899 --> 00:07:24,444
- Atoy, enough-
- [giggles]

216
00:07:24,527 --> 00:07:25,778
We're old already.

217
00:07:25,862 --> 00:07:27,405
- There’s no courting happening.
- Ah, geez.

218
00:07:27,488 --> 00:07:29,198
Oh, no. Actually, it's not just a spark.

219
00:07:29,282 --> 00:07:30,408
It's like real electricity,

220
00:07:30,491 --> 00:07:31,534
like 220 volts!

221
00:07:31,617 --> 00:07:33,661
Atoy: You can really feel it from there.

222
00:07:33,744 --> 00:07:35,204
That kind of electricity
really goes through.

223
00:07:36,205 --> 00:07:37,290
- Huh?
- We're old already.

224
00:07:37,373 --> 00:07:38,875
There’s no courting like that.

225
00:07:38,958 --> 00:07:39,959
Atoy: So, what?

226
00:07:40,042 --> 00:07:42,545
Godmother, age doesn't matter.

227
00:07:42,628 --> 00:07:45,339
Love doesn't choose an age, okay.

228
00:07:45,423 --> 00:07:47,341
You might be forgetting, huh,

229
00:07:47,425 --> 00:07:49,177
I have a husband.

230
00:07:49,886 --> 00:07:50,720
So what?

231
00:07:50,803 --> 00:07:52,096
Where is he?

232
00:07:52,180 --> 00:07:54,432
After what he did to you and Karla?

233
00:07:54,515 --> 00:07:56,392
After he evaded the law,

234
00:07:56,476 --> 00:07:57,894
Where is he? Where's your husband?

235
00:07:58,436 --> 00:08:01,439
And, Miss Cita, love only
comes once in a while.

236
00:08:01,522 --> 00:08:03,024
You're not stepping on anyone.

237
00:08:03,107 --> 00:08:04,859
So just be open.

238
00:08:04,942 --> 00:08:06,819
Ame, is that you? Huh? [chuckles]

239
00:08:06,903 --> 00:08:09,530
- Audrey: Atoy!
- [Cita gasps]

240
00:08:11,032 --> 00:08:11,574
Yes, love?

241
00:08:11,657 --> 00:08:12,700
Who is this woman

242
00:08:12,783 --> 00:08:13,826
and why are you hugging each other?!

243
00:08:13,910 --> 00:08:17,914
[tense music playing]

244
00:08:23,544 --> 00:08:25,087
It’s…

245
00:08:25,171 --> 00:08:27,757
[rousing music playing]

246
00:08:27,840 --> 00:08:29,300
Her name is Georgia.

247
00:08:29,383 --> 00:08:31,010
WOMEN: Georgia?!

248
00:08:31,093 --> 00:08:31,886
Yes.

249
00:08:32,762 --> 00:08:33,721
Atoy: I me-- I met--

250
00:08:33,804 --> 00:08:35,389
And why were you
hugging each other?!

251
00:08:35,473 --> 00:08:37,892
No. We were not hugging.

252
00:08:38,935 --> 00:08:39,810
No, I-- I--

253
00:08:39,894 --> 00:08:41,562
I met her earlier.

254
00:08:41,646 --> 00:08:43,397
I was at the coffee shop.

255
00:08:43,481 --> 00:08:44,690
Then when I was leaving the coffee shop,

256
00:08:44,774 --> 00:08:46,150
she was leaving too,

257
00:08:46,234 --> 00:08:47,360
Atoy: sh-- sh-- she stum-- stumbled.

258
00:08:47,443 --> 00:08:49,487
And then, I just helped her.

259
00:08:50,238 --> 00:08:51,322
Okay? I mean, look at it.

260
00:08:51,405 --> 00:08:52,782
I didn't hug her, I just helped her.

261
00:08:52,865 --> 00:08:54,951
And it just so happened
that Paldo was there.

262
00:08:55,034 --> 00:08:56,577
He took a picture because
they were keeping tabs

263
00:08:56,661 --> 00:09:00,373
on their client's husband,
the client of the Children Of Thread.

264
00:09:00,456 --> 00:09:00,957
Yes.

265
00:09:01,040 --> 00:09:02,375
So, this is their evidence?

266
00:09:02,458 --> 00:09:03,834
This is evidence.

267
00:09:03,918 --> 00:09:05,086
Then why was it cut?

268
00:09:05,670 --> 00:09:07,380
Uh-- uh,

269
00:09:07,463 --> 00:09:08,881
so there wouldn't be any trouble.

270
