to perform with me,

549
00:19:13,610 --> 00:19:15,404
based on my research.

550
00:19:16,446 --> 00:19:18,198
Sir, confirmed.

551
00:19:18,282 --> 00:19:19,074
Everything set?

552
00:19:19,908 --> 00:19:20,993
[chuckles]

553
00:19:21,076 --> 00:19:22,452
Put it on speaker, put it on speaker!

554
00:19:22,536 --> 00:19:23,954
Put it on speaker, put it on speaker.

555
00:19:24,037 --> 00:19:25,414
Too late. I already dropped the call.

556
00:19:25,497 --> 00:19:26,915
Mmm, you're just pretending

557
00:19:26,999 --> 00:19:27,958
- you were talking to someone.
- Nice one!

558
00:19:28,041 --> 00:19:28,917
I'm good.

559
00:19:29,418 --> 00:19:30,043
Nice one, girl.

560
00:19:30,127 --> 00:19:30,627
I'm good.

561
00:19:30,711 --> 00:19:32,171
[playful music playing]

562
00:19:32,254 --> 00:19:34,214
[SIGHS] You know, Hailey…

563
00:19:34,965 --> 00:19:38,010
I thought Ibyang and I
would be best friends forever

564
00:19:38,093 --> 00:19:39,386
because we're sisters now.

565
00:19:39,928 --> 00:19:41,096
Janine: Apparently not.

566
00:19:41,180 --> 00:19:42,514
Well, real talk.

567
00:19:43,515 --> 00:19:45,142
Ibyang isn't your real sister.

568
00:19:45,642 --> 00:19:47,436
Anytime, she can choose to let you go.

569
00:19:48,103 --> 00:19:49,396
Hailey: Don't be sad, Janine.

570
00:19:50,564 --> 00:19:52,191
I'm here for you.

571
00:19:52,274 --> 00:19:54,860
No matter what,
we'll always be best friends.

572
00:19:54,943 --> 00:19:55,819
We're solid!

573
00:19:57,237 --> 00:19:59,198
Team Ja-Ley forever?

574
00:19:59,281 --> 00:20:00,741
Team Ja-Ley forever.

575
00:20:00,824 --> 00:20:05,245
BOTH: Team Ja-Ley forever!

576
00:20:05,329 --> 00:20:06,997
[rousing music playing]

577
00:20:07,497 --> 00:20:11,627
You know, I wish you had
been my real sister instead, Hailey.

578
00:20:11,710 --> 00:20:12,461
[heavy music playing]

579
00:20:12,544 --> 00:20:13,670
Janine: Yeah.

580
00:20:14,171 --> 00:20:17,716
[music continues]

581
00:20:18,926 --> 00:20:19,551
Yummy.

582
00:20:20,552 --> 00:20:21,220
Delicious.

583
00:20:21,303 --> 00:20:21,929
[music fades]

584
00:20:22,012 --> 00:20:24,223
[FOOTSTEPS TAPPING]

585
00:20:24,306 --> 00:20:25,724
My cooking is good, right?

586
00:20:25,807 --> 00:20:27,017
- Mmm.
- Good morning.

587
00:20:27,643 --> 00:20:28,393
[TELEVISION BLIPS]

588
00:20:29,686 --> 00:20:30,729
Ibyang: Good morning!

589
00:20:30,812 --> 00:20:32,272
Audrey: Good morning, my loves!

590
00:20:32,856 --> 00:20:34,191
What's the tastiest thing there?

591
00:20:34,274 --> 00:20:34,942
This one.

592
00:20:35,025 --> 00:20:36,068
Uhm, the chicken nuggets.

593
00:20:37,194 --> 00:20:39,112
Ibyang: Ah, Mama.

594
00:20:39,196 --> 00:20:39,821
Hmm?

595
00:20:40,656 --> 00:20:43,367
Where is Tatoy?

596
00:20:44,159 --> 00:20:46,328
Mmm, he left early, sweetheart.

597
00:20:46,411 --> 00:20:48,205
He went to see a client.

598
00:20:48,705 --> 00:20:52,542
Uhm, Mommy, can we invite

599
00:20:52,626 --> 00:20:54,253
Hailey here to our house?

600
00:20:54,920 --> 00:20:57,214
We're going to have a tea party.

601
00:20:57,297 --> 00:20:58,215
Of course.

602
00:20:59,216 --> 00:21:00,759
But what, just the two of you?

603
00:21:00,842 --> 00:21:02,302
Your sister isn't included?

604
00:21:02,386 --> 00:21:03,553
[suspicious music playing]

605
00:21:04,179 --> 00:21:06,765
Uhm, she's included too.

606
00:21:07,474 --> 00:21:09,810
That is, if she wants to.

607
00:21:09,893 --> 00:21:10,769
Ah.

608
00:21:11,395 --> 00:21:12,771
Can I also invite someone?

609
00:21:12,854 --> 00:21:15,816
Ah, because I'm calling Wanbol.

610
00:21:15,899 --> 00:21:18,318
We're doing a group project.

611
00:21:19,027 --> 00:21:20,195
[music fades]

612
00:21:20,279 --> 00:21:20,946
Of course.

613
00:21:21,029 --> 00:21:23,365
Huh? But Wanbol smells so bad.

614
00:21:23,865 --> 00:21:26,118
He always smells like fish. Gross.

615
00:21:26,201 --> 00:21:27,703
Janine!

616
00:21:27,786 --> 00:21:29,371
Audrey: That's not good behavior.

617
00:21:29,454 --> 00:21:30,872
Don't talk like that.

618
00:21:30,956 --> 00:21:31,581
Janine: But it's true.

619
00:21:31,665 --> 00:21:34,251
That's not nice.

620
00:21:35,502 --> 00:21:37,337
[suspicious music playing]

621
00:21:37,421 --> 00:21:38,463
REPORTER ON TV: Ma'am, how much is

622
00:21:38,547 --> 00:21:40,048
a kilo of tilapia now?

623
00:21:40,132 --> 00:21:42,718
[muffled chattering]

624
00:21:43,385 --> 00:21:47,347
[music continues]

625
00:21:59,651 --> 00:22:00,319
[music fades]

626
00:22:00,402 --> 00:22:01,737
It looks like churros.

627
00:22:01,820 --> 00:22:03,322
Oh, ready? On set?

628
00:22:03,405 --> 00:22:06,366
[CAR DOOR CLOSES] Uno, are the disguises
in the back already?

629
00:22:06,450 --> 00:22:07,826
They're here in the back seat, Sir.

630
00:22:08,368 --> 00:22:09,077
Yes, Sir!

631
00:22:09,161 --> 00:22:09,661
All set.

632
00:22:09,745 --> 00:22:12,289
[soft rock music playing]

633
00:22:12,372 --> 00:22:14,041
Is that my reggae hat you're using?

634
00:22:14,124 --> 00:22:16,001
Ah, y-- yes.

635
00:22:16,084 --> 00:22:18,253
Mmm-mmm. No. Well, uh, I just borrowed it,

636
00:22:18,337 --> 00:22:18,837
I was just trying it on.

637
00:22:18,920 --> 00:22:20,380
- It suits you, because…
- Atoy: Suits me?

638
00:22:20,464 --> 00:22:21,506
♪ But you, oh, oh ♪

639
00:22:21,590 --> 00:22:22,341
Wait, wait, wait.

640
00:22:22,424 --> 00:22:23,800
Did you ask your wife for permission?

641
00:22:23,884 --> 00:22:26,053
[rousing music playing]

642
00:22:26,636 --> 00:22:28,263
[CAR ENGINE STARTS]

643
00:22:29,014 --> 00:22:29,848
Hello?

644
00:22:29,931 --> 00:22:30,891
[pensive music playing]

645
00:22:30,974 --> 00:22:32,768
I have eyes on Atoy Padua.

646
00:22:32,851 --> 00:22:33,435
Elias: Huh?

647
00:22:34,186 --> 00:22:35,896
What? Yo-- you've got Atoy's eyes?

648
00:22:35,979 --> 00:22:37,522
How did that happen?

649
00:22:37,606 --> 00:22:39,316
What I mean, Sir,

650
00:22:39,399 --> 00:22:40,442
is that I've spotted him.

651
00:22:41,234 --> 00:22:42,069
Well, well!

652
00:22:42,152 --> 00:22:43,070
[smirks]

653
00:22:43,862 --> 00:22:44,905
Very good.

654
00:22:44,988 --> 00:22:46,907
Okay, here's what you're going to do.

655
00:22:47,699 --> 00:22:50,035
Don't take your eyes off Atoy.

656
00:22:50,118 --> 00:22:51,620
Do we understand each other?

657
00:22:51,703 --> 00:22:52,454
Copy, Sir.

658
00:22:52,537 --> 00:22:53,497
[RETCHES]

659
00:22:54,289 --> 00:22:55,373
It's hot.

660
00:22:55,457 --> 00:22:59,169
[soft rock music playing]

661
00:23:01,296 --> 00:23:03,465
[CAR REVVING]

662
00:23:07,844 --> 00:23:08,386
[music fades]

663
00:23:10,013 --> 00:23:16,019
[rock music playing]

664
00:23:20,190 --> 00:23:20,941
Garrett!

665
00:23:21,024 --> 00:23:21,650
Garrett: Hey!

666
00:23:21,733 --> 00:23:22,651
How was your trip?

667
00:23:22,734 --> 00:23:24,611
[chuckles softly]

668
00:23:24,694 --> 00:23:25,987
You know, thanks, okay.

669
00:23:26,071 --> 00:23:27,739
You're really reliable.

670
00:23:27,823 --> 00:23:29,199
You're the best.

671
00:23:29,282 --> 00:23:31,743
Oh, wh-- it looks like
you're missing someone?

672
00:23:31,827 --> 00:23:34,037
Ah, right. Sorry, bro.

673
00:23:34,121 --> 00:23:37,582
Boss, Sir, our companion Uno…

674
00:23:37,666 --> 00:23:39,876
his stomach got a little upset.

675
00:23:39,960 --> 00:23:41,878
So, he had to rush to the ER first.

676
00:23:41,962 --> 00:23:43,296
But don't worry,

677
00:23:43,380 --> 00:23:44,965
we found a replacement.

678
00:23:45,966 --> 00:23:46,633
Paldo!

679
00:23:47,259 --> 00:23:48,093
BOTH: Yeah!

680
00:23:48,176 --> 00:23:49,344
Eyy!

681
00:23:49,427 --> 00:23:50,512
[chuckling]

682
00:23:50,595 --> 00:23:51,304
Jesabel: This is exciting.

683
00:23:51,388 --> 00:23:52,514
Oh, huh.

684
00:23:52,597 --> 00:23:53,765
You can really count on this guy.

685
00:23:54,641 --> 00:23:56,601
Sir, don't worry.

686
00:23:56,685 --> 00:23:58,145
Paldo is really talented,

687
00:23:58,228 --> 00:23:59,104
he really plays music,

688
00:23:59,187 --> 00:24:00,313
and he studied

689
00:24:00,397 --> 00:24:01,982
the material we'll be doing later.

690
00:24:02,065 --> 00:24:03,233
It’s easy-peasy.

691
00:24:03,316 --> 00:24:05,110
Right-- okay. Don’t worry,

692
00:24:05,193 --> 00:24:06,153
this is easy, bro.

693
00:24:06,236 --> 00:24:07,445
This is easy, just remember,

694
00:24:07,529 --> 00:24:10,782
just support the band's percussion.

695
00:24:11,741 --> 00:24:12,868
Rumba and shakers.

696
00:24:12,951 --> 00:24:14,786
Just like we practiced last night.

697
00:24:14,870 --> 00:24:16,121
That's it, just support.

698
00:24:16,204 --> 00:24:17,080
- So, you already know what to do.
- Yeah, yeah.

699
00:24:17,622 --> 00:24:19,082
Ah, but, Sir, uhm…

700
00:24:19,166 --> 00:24:21,334
before everything,
before we start, there's--

701
00:24:22,294 --> 00:24:25,589
Not that you asked, I'm a tailor, sir.

702
00:24:25,672 --> 00:24:27,507
- Yeah.
- Yeah. He's a tailor!

703
00:24:27,591 --> 00:24:29,009
Yeah, I-- I actually have something

704
00:24:29,092 --> 00:24:30,093
I'd like to give you, Sir.

705
00:24:30,177 --> 00:24:31,761
Would that be okay?

706
00:24:31,845 --> 00:24:33,805
I have a plan for a gi-- gift!

707
00:24:33,889 --> 00:24:35,182
Yeah, I like that!

708
00:24:35,265 --> 00:24:35,932
That's great.

709
00:24:36,016 --> 00:24:37,350
Ju-- just make the suit
reggae-inspired, okay.

710
00:24:37,434 --> 00:24:38,810
Reggae all the way, Sir!

711
00:24:38,894 --> 00:24:40,353
- Ah, would you like it, uhm…
- Nice, nice, nice.

712
00:24:40,437 --> 00:24:42,147
Loose or tight?

713
00:24:42,230 --> 00:24:43,231
I can do anything.

714
00:24:43,315 --> 00:24:44,232
It should be a little loose, so--

715
00:24:44,316 --> 00:24:45,192
A little loose. Okay.

716
00:24:45,275 --> 00:24:46,359
So, we can move around.

717
00:24:46,443 --> 00:24:48,278
22, 22. Okay.

718
00:24:48,361 --> 00:24:49,529
[CAMERA SHUTTER SNAPS]

719
00:24:49,613 --> 00:24:51,406
Atoy: We'll make this
a little looser, and then…

720
00:24:51,489 --> 00:24:54,284
this one, I-- I'll probably make it two,

721
00:24:54,367 --> 00:24:55,202
there's one 23.

722
00:24:55,285 --> 00:24:56,703
What is that for?

723
00:24:56,786 --> 00:24:59,122
Ah, nothing. Just a receipt for Audrey.

724
00:24:59,206 --> 00:24:59,915
Ah, no, uh…

725
00:24:59,998 --> 00:25:03,501
It's just that sometimes
the notes get lost here,

726
00:25:03,585 --> 00:25:05,003
so I just read them from here.

727
00:25:05,086 --> 00:25:05,837
- Atoy: Ah, that's true.
- Right, right.

728
00:25:05,921 --> 00:25:06,588
23?

729
00:25:07,339 --> 00:25:08,465
- Yeah, 23.
- Yeah.

730
00:25:08,548 --> 00:25:10,008
Atoy: Chest, okay.

731
00:25:10,091 --> 00:25:12,844
Sorry, Sir. Chest.

732
00:25:12,928 --> 00:25:13,803
[chuckling]

733
00:25:14,638 --> 00:25:15,764
- 41, 41.
- 41.

734
00:25:15,847 --> 00:25:17,474
[music fades]

735
00:25:17,557 --> 00:25:18,642
Elias on the phone: Oh, hello?

736
00:25:19,226 --> 00:25:20,602
Did you miss me already?

737
00:25:22,312 --> 00:25:23,063
No, Sir.

738
00:25:23,563 --> 00:25:25,190
But I have an update on Padua.

739
00:25:25,732 --> 00:25:28,944
He's here at Indigo Pearl Beach Resort.

740
00:25:29,027 --> 00:25:31,780
Looks like some kind of
transaction is taking place inside.

741
00:25:31,863 --> 00:25:35,242
And since, uh, you can't conduct

742
00:25:35,325 --> 00:25:37,911
a private investigation without…

743
00:25:37,994 --> 00:25:39,371
Elias on the phone: a legal warrant,

744
00:25:39,454 --> 00:25:41,623
you'll need access, right?

745
00:25:41,706 --> 00:25:43,750
Yes, Sir. I definitely need it.

746
00:25:43,833 --> 00:25:45,502
Can you find a way?

747
00:25:46,628 --> 00:25:48,755
I got it, of course!

748
00:25:49,256 --> 00:25:50,882
I know someone at Indigo Pearl

749
00:25:50,966 --> 00:25:52,884
who'll help you.

750
00:25:52,968 --> 00:25:54,844
Just wait, okay? I got you. Okay?

751
00:25:56,638 --> 00:25:57,806
Ah, thank you, Sir.

752
00:25:57,889 --> 00:25:58,431
[THUDS SOFTLY]

753
00:25:58,515 --> 00:25:59,057
Samir: Oh.

754
00:25:59,140 --> 00:26:00,809
[tense music playing]

755
00:26:01,309 --> 00:26:02,602
Apologies. Here.

756
00:26:04,312 --> 00:26:05,313
[music fades]

757
00:26:05,397 --> 00:26:08,149
[ELECTRONIC BLIPPING]

758
00:26:09,776 --> 00:26:14,197
[intense music playing]

759
00:26:16,533 --> 00:26:18,118
We've got a problem, Audrey is here.

760
00:26:18,201 --> 00:26:19,452
Oka is with her.

761
00:26:19,536 --> 00:26:21,454
Atoy: I knew they were
coming here to the reception.

762
00:26:23,206 --> 00:26:24,124
Excuse me.

763
00:26:24,207 --> 00:26:26,251
Audrey: Are you Georgia?

764
00:26:26,334 --> 00:26:28,878
I'm Audrey Padua.

765
00:26:28,962 --> 00:26:29,546
Yes?

766
00:26:30,088 --> 00:26:31,506
Anthony Padua's wife.

767
00:26:32,549 --> 00:26:34,467
Bro, Chanty is at the tailoring shop.

768
00:26:34,551 --> 00:26:36,219
That's where Karla and I are meeting too.

769
00:26:36,303 --> 00:26:37,095
Chanty?

770
00:26:37,178 --> 00:26:38,305
What are you doing here?

771
00:26:38,388 --> 00:26:41,016
I have someone I'm meeting today.

772
00:26:41,099 --> 00:26:42,225
Who?

773
00:26:42,309 --> 00:26:44,352
Any, uh, suspicious prospects?

774
00:26:45,061 --> 00:26:46,146
I have a lot of prospects,

775
00:26:46,229 --> 00:26:48,690
but none of them are suspicious.

776
00:26:48,773 --> 00:26:51,192
[upbeat reggae music playing]

777
00:26:51,276 --> 00:26:54,821
Guys, guys, Audrey is at 10 o'clock.

778
00:26:54,904 --> 00:26:58,491
[tense music playing]

779
00:26:58,575 --> 00:26:59,534
[THUDS] Ouch!

780
00:26:59,617 --> 00:27:00,869
[groans]

781
00:27:00,952 --> 00:27:02,162
Atoy.

782
00:27:02,245 --> 00:27:05,332
[music swells]

783
00:27:06,041 --> 00:27:06,916
[music fades]
